### Styling Best Practices
- Use Tailwind utility classes, avoid inline styles
- Use responsive modifiers: `sm:`, `md:`, `lg:`, etc.
- Group related classes: layout, spacing, colors, typography
- Use custom colors from theme, not arbitrary values

## State Management

### Context Providers
```javascript
// DataContext: Global data from API
import { useData } from '@/app/context/DataContext';

// LanguageContext: Language preferences
import { LanguageProvider } from '@/app/context/LanguageContext';

// FareHarborContext: Booking integration
import { FareHarborProvider } from '@/app/context/FareHarborContext';
```

### Usage Pattern
```javascript
'use client';
import { useData } from '@/app/context/DataContext';

export default function Component() {
  const { data, loading, error } = useData();
  
  if (loading) return <div>Loading...</div>;
  if (error) return <div>Error loading data</div>;
  
  return <div>{data.settings[0].site_title}</div>;
}
```

## API Routes & Backend

### API Structure
- Located in `app/api/` directory
- Use route handlers (`route.js` files)
- Handle POST requests for forms and actions
- Return JSON responses with proper status codes

### Common API Routes
- `/api/send-email` - Email sending via Nodemailer
- `/api/payment` - Payment processing
- `/api/subscribe` - Newsletter subscriptions
- `/api/get-data` - Fetch yacht data
- `/api/revalidate` - On-demand revalidation

### Error Handling
```javascript
try {
  // API logic
  return Response.json({ success: true, data });
} catch (error) {
  console.error('Error:', error);
  return Response.json(
    { success: false, error: 'Error message' },
    { status: 500 }
  );
}
```

## Third-Party Integrations

### FareHarbor (Booking System)
- Load via `FareHarborLoader` component
- Use `FareHarborProvider` for context
- Load calendar widget with `FareHarborCalendar` component

### Payment Gateways
- Tabby (Buy now, pay later)
- RakBank payment integration
- Handle payment callbacks and webhooks

### Email (Nodemailer)
- Send booking confirmations
- Send contact form submissions
- Handle email templates

### WhatsApp
- Use dynamic WhatsApp links from settings API
- Format: `https://wa.link/[code]`
- Display WhatsApp icon for contact

### Google Tag Manager
- Loaded in root layout
- Track page views and conversions
- GTM ID: GTM-NPBPZQ2

## Domain-Specific Rules

### Yacht Charter Entities
- **Yacht Rentals**: Private yacht bookings
- **Yacht Trips**: Shared tours and experiences
- **Offers**: Special promotions and packages
- **Events**: F1 racing, New Year, special occasions
- **Water Sports**: Additional activities
- **Yachts for Sale**: Yacht sales listings

### Booking Flow
1. Browse yachts/trips
2. View details with image carousel
3. Check availability via FareHarbor
4. Fill booking form (Modal/Modal2/Modal3)
5. Payment processing
6. Confirmation email

### Contact Methods
- WhatsApp button (primary)
- Contact form (secondary)
- Phone number link
- Email link
- All contact info from settings API

### Forms & Validation
- Use `react-phone-input-2` for phone inputs
- Validate email addresses
- Validate dates with `react-date-range` or `react-multi-date-picker`
- Show loading states during submission
- Display success/error messages

## Performance & SEO

### Image Optimization
- Use `.webp` format for images
- Store images in `/public/images/`
- Use Next.js Image component with proper dimensions
- Set `priority={true}` for above-fold images
- Use responsive images with srcSet

### Metadata & SEO
```javascript
// layout.tsx or page.tsx
export async function generateMetadata({ params }) {
  const { locale } = await params;
  
  return {
    title: 'Page Title',
    description: 'Page description',
    canonical: 'https://www.centauruscharter.com/path',
    // ... more metadata
  };
}
```

### Caching Strategy
- Static assets: 1 year cache (immutable)
- HTML pages: 60s browser, 1h CDN, stale-while-revalidate
- API routes: No cache by default
- Images: 30 days cache (configured in next.config.ts)

### Performance Best Practices
- Preconnect to external domains (Adobe Fonts, FareHarbor)
- Lazy load below-fold content
- Use loading states for async operations
- Minimize client-side JavaScript
- Prefer Server Components when possible

## Error Handling & User Experience

### Loading States
```javascript
const [loading, setLoading] = useState(false);

const handleSubmit = async () => {
  setLoading(true);
  try {
    await submitForm();
  } catch (error) {
    console.error(error);
  } finally {
    setLoading(false);
  }
};
```

### Error Messages
- Show user-friendly error messages
- Log detailed errors to console
- Provide fallback UI for failed data fetches
- Handle 404s with custom not-found page

### Modals
- Modal: Basic modal for forms
- Modal2: Enhanced modal with custom logic
- Modal3: Alternative modal variant
- Close modals on successful submission
- Handle modal state with useState

### Form Validation
- Required field validation
- Email format validation
- Phone number validation with libphonenumber-js
- Date range validation
- Display validation errors inline

## Special Page Types

### Landing Pages
- Different navbar (LandingNavbar vs Navbar)
- No footer components
- Optimized for conversions
- Example: `/landing-abu-dhabi-race-yacht-charter`

### Detection Pattern
```javascript
const isLandingPage = currentPath?.includes('landing-') || false;

{isLandingPage ? <LandingNavbar /> : <Navbar />}
{isLandingPage ? null : <FirstFooter />}
```

### Checkout Pages
- Multi-step checkout flow
- Payment widget integration
- Order confirmation
- Dynamic routing: `/checkout/[slug]`

## Important Constraints

### DO NOT
- Remove 'use client' from existing client components
- Use `next/link` directly (use `app/i18n/routing` instead)
- Hardcode user-facing text (use translations)
- Use inline styles (use Tailwind classes)
- Modify .prettierrc or eslint.config.js without reason
- Break backwards compatibility with existing .js components
- Remove existing custom Tailwind classes
- Change WhatsApp/contact info (must come from settings API)

### ALWAYS
- Test changes with multiple locales (en, ar, ru, zh)
- Await params in Server Components (Next.js 15 requirement)
- Use proper TypeScript types when in .tsx files
- Optimize images with Next.js Image component
- Handle loading and error states
- Validate user inputs
- Use semantic HTML
- Add proper alt text to images
- Follow existing component patterns

### CODE REVIEW CHECKLIST
- [ ] Uses correct imports from `@/app/i18n/routing`
- [ ] Client components have 'use client' directive
- [ ] All user-facing text uses translations
- [ ] Images use Next.js Image component
- [ ] Proper error handling and loading states
- [ ] Responsive design with Tailwind breakpoints
- [ ] Follows Prettier formatting (2 spaces, single quotes)
- [ ] No console.log in production code (console.error is OK)
- [ ] Proper TypeScript types (if .tsx file)
- [ ] SEO metadata included (if page route)

## Common Patterns

### Page Component Template
```javascript
// Server Component
import { useTranslations } from 'next-intl';
import { getTranslations } from 'next-intl/server';
import Navbar from '@/app/components/Navbar';

export async function generateMetadata({ params }) {
  const { locale } = await params;
  const t = await getTranslations({ locale });
  
  return {
    title: t('page.title'),
    description: t('page.description'),
  };
}

export default async function Page({ params }) {
  const { locale } = await params;
  const data = await fetchData();
  
  return (
    <div>
      <h1>{data.title}</h1>
      <ClientComponent data={data} />
    </div>
  );
}
```

### Client Component Template
```javascript
'use client';
import { useState } from 'react';
import { useTranslations } from 'next-intl';
import { Link } from '@/app/i18n/routing';

export default function Component({ data }) {
  const t = useTranslations();
  const [state, setState] = useState(false);
  
  return (
    <div className="container mx-auto px-4">
      <h2>{t('component.title')}</h2>
      <Link href="/about">{t('nav.about')}</Link>
    </div>
  );
}
```

### API Route Template
```javascript
export async function POST(request) {
  try {
    const body = await request.json();
    
    // Validate input
    if (!body.email) {
      return Response.json(
        { success: false, error: 'Email is required' },
        { status: 400 }
      );
    }
    
    // Process request
    const result = await processData(body);
    
    return Response.json({ success: true, data: result });
  } catch (error) {
    console.error('API Error:', error);
    return Response.json(
      { success: false, error: error.message },
      { status: 500 }
    );
  }
}
```

## Development Workflow

### Running the Project
```bash
npm run dev          # Start development server
npm run build        # Build for production
npm run start        # Start production server
npm run lint         # Run ESLint
npm run format       # Format with Prettier
npm run format:check # Check formatting
```

### Environment
- Development: http://localhost:3000
- Production: https://www.centauruscharter.com
- Node.js 18+ required

### Git Workflow
- Commit with meaningful messages
- Test with multiple locales before committing
- Run linter before pushing
- Keep changes focused and atomic

